<h2><a id="Presentació" name="Presentació"></a>Presentation and options</h2>

<p>This application allows you to obtain the information of the internal metadata  of the JPEG2000 format, to import a JPEG2000 to a JPEG format (grey or RGB,  depending on the JPEG2000 file) or to extract between one and three IMG  bands of a JPEG2000.Thereby, depending on your interest the program allows you to execute different options:</p>

<p>When the JPEG2000 images have been compressed without loss, it can have  sense to recover the images as IMG files to analyse them, although these  file might need much more disc space than the original images, and if the  images need more than 2 Gbyte for spectral band it could be impossible to  convert. So, the application has the following options:</p>

<!--Aquí inicia la part corresponent a les opcions de de la MSA. Aquesta part s'ha d'editar desde el document WPS (aplicacio.mps).-->
<span id="wpsopcions"/>
<!--Aquí acaba la part corresponent a les opcions de de la MSA editable de el WPS.--> 

<p>The JPEG2000 files are rasters highly compressed  thanks to the use of transformed wavelet. JPEG2000 uses typically degrading  compression (it also named unconservative, with loss, or lossy), for being  the one that more strongly compresses the image; despite this unconserving  character, the images usually have a visual aspect very similar to the  original ones, unless they have been generated at compression levels  extremely raised; this is an important difference with regard to the JPEG  conventional format, which starts presenting visual gadgetry at minor levels  of compression. On the other hand, the JPEG format can also compress in an  efficient way even without degrading the values of the original image  (conserving compression, without loss, or lossless), even if in this case  the levels of compression are not so high.</p>

